{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Inherited from ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sequence.lazy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lazy","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LazySequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s12LazySequenceV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"lazy","externalID":"s:STsE4lazys12LazySequenceVyxGvp::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"Cliques","relatedModules":["Swift"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lazy"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LazySequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s12LazySequenceV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"extendedModule":"Swift","role":"symbol"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/lazy"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/lazy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques/lazy":{"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques\/lazy","role":"symbol","title":"lazy","type":"topic","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lazy","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s12LazySequenceV","text":"LazySequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques\/lazy","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/MaximalCliques":{"title":"MaximalCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","abstract":[{"text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}]},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques","abstract":[],"title":"Cliques","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/cliques"}}}